{"id": "EUVD-2026-87329", "enisaUuid": "d7a43f61-9923-37c3-9224-4d314b525db7", "description": "On Windows, PHP's filesystem and stream APIs do not reject reserved device names such as CON, PRN, AUX, NUL, COM1 to COM9, LPT1 to LPT9, CONIN$ and CONOUT$ when they appear as a component of a path. An attacker-controlled filename therefore reaches CreateFileW() and opens a device instead of the regular file the application expected, which can block or hang the request and exhaust worker processes.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T20:18:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-25T20:43:34", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:H", "references": ["https://github.com/php/php-src/security/advisories/GHSA-9f67-6fw4-hpfp"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-17545"], "assigner": "php", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "43cd405c-1fc5-34d7-bb6d-4c45776dc691", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.2.* <8.2.34"}, {"id": "5cc6c0ec-7c1a-36bf-867e-5aa151d0ccbd", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.3.* <8.3.35"}, {"id": "75feff77-ba3c-3311-ba6a-d2cfd211646a", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.4.* <8.4.26"}, {"id": "e45f66d9-2a13-3b58-855d-6e73ed1aa648", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.5.* <8.5.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c74ac235-f9f3-3320-812d-10b27c905218", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}], "isExploited": false}